  "zones": [
    {
      "name": "Jezero crater",
      "card": "01 / 06\nJEZERO CRATER\nPerseverance\nN ↑\n3.4 km\n\nAn ancient lake crater with a river delta. Perseverance has explored it since 2021 and sealed the first samples meant for return to Earth.\n\nWater 3.5 wt%\nRadiation 0.69 mSv/day · est.\n18.49° N · 77.43° E\nOrbital image",
      "travel": true
    },
    {
      "name": "Gale crater",
      "card": "02 / 06\nGALE CRATER\nCuriosity\nN ↑\n3.4 km\n\nA 154 km crater around Mount Sharp. Curiosity has climbed its layered rocks since 2012, reading the record of long-lived ancient lakes.\n\nWater 5.4 wt%\nRadiation 0.64 mSv/day · measured\n4.73° S · 137.39° E\nOrbital image",
      "travel": true
    },
    {
      "name": "Gusev crater",
      "card": "03 / 06\nGUSEV CRATER\nSpirit\nN ↑\n3.4 km\n\nA crater once thought to hold a lake. Spirit drove from its landing site to the Columbia Hills and Home Plate between 2004 and 2010.\n\nWater 7.3 wt%\nRadiation 0.70 mSv/day · est.\n14.58° S · 175.50° E\nOrbital image",
      "travel": true
    },
    {
      "name": "Elysium Planitia",
      "card": "04 / 06\nELYSIUM PLANITIA\nInSight\nN ↑\n3.4 km\n\nA smooth volcanic plain chosen as a safe, flat site for the InSight lander, which listened to marsquakes from 2018 to 2022.\n\nWater 5.2 wt%\nRadiation 0.69 mSv/day · est.\n4.50° N · 135.62° E\nOrbital image",
      "travel": true
    },
    {
      "name": "Meridiani Planum",
      "card": "05 / 06\nMERIDIANI PLANUM\nOpportunity\nN ↑\n3.4 km\n\nHematite-rich plains. Opportunity drove more than 45 km here from 2004 to 2018 and spent its last years on the rim of Endeavour crater.\n\nWater 5.3 wt%\nRadiation 0.71 mSv/day · est.\n2.27° S · 5.37° W\nOrbital image",
      "travel": true
    },
    {
      "name": "Valles Marineris",
      "card": "06 / 06\nVALLES MARINERIS\nNo landed mission\nN ↑\n3.4 km\n\nMelas Chasma, part of the largest canyon system in the Solar System. No spacecraft has ever landed here.\n\nWater 3.4 wt%\nRadiation 0.67 mSv/day · est.\n12.87° S · 69.06° W\nOrbital image",
      "travel": true
    }
  ],
